<title>USA: Tele-Comms wants out-of-market football.</title>
<headline>Tele-Comms wants out-of-market football.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc wants to be able to offer its cable television customers a package of National Football League out-of-market games, TCI executives said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to talk to them about giving our customers a fair shake,&quot; Bob Thomson, TCI senior vice president and spokesman told a teleconference call held to explain the company's rate increases.</p>
<p>Direct broadcast satellite (DBS) competitors are able to offer such packages.  Thomson said in the past the NFL has cited resistance from local broadcasters as a reason for not offering the expanded games package to cable television companies.</p>
</text>
